% ============================================================================
% aqi-category-color.query.adj — a worked recall over the environment
% aqi-category-color library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what color is a
% hazardous air-quality day?": it states no environment fact of its own —
% it only `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine
% resolves each `?` against the `aqi_category_color` rows and returns the
% color + the table's source/locator/trust. Every category the parent
% table names has a color in the cited spans, so this table never abstains.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli aqi-category-color.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "aqi-category-color.adj"

? aqi_category_color(hazardous, $Color)              % expect maroon
? aqi_category_color($Category, orange)               % expect unhealthy_for_sensitive_groups
? aqi_category_color(good, $Color)                     % expect green
